# Android / production-build API location.
#
# Why this file and not .env:
#   Vite loads `.env` in EVERY mode, so putting VITE_API_URL there would also
#   change the browser dev server — it would stop using the Vite proxy and hit
#   this address directly. `.env.production.local` is loaded only by
#   `vite build`, which is exactly what `npm run mobile:sync` runs. So the web
#   dev workflow is untouched and the phone still gets an absolute URL.
#
# This file is gitignored (.env.*.local) and never reaches Vercel.
#
# The deployed API on Render. Absolute and https, so it works over mobile data
# as well as Wi-Fi and survives a release build — a release APK cannot send
# cleartext HTTP, so the old http://192.168.x.x LAN address could never have
# worked outside a debug build on the same network. See MOBILE.md.
VITE_API_URL=https://snowfall-server-p974.onrender.com

# --- If login still fails with "Network error" ---
# 1. The Render service must be RUNNING. A suspended service answers every
#    request with 503 and the app reports a network error.
#      curl https://snowfall-server-p974.onrender.com/health   → {"ok":true}
#    (The old snowfall-server-zot5 service is SUSPENDED — do not point at it.)
# 1b. CORS: the server must allow the WebView origin `https://localhost`.
#    This needs the NATIVE_ORIGINS list in server/src/config/env.ts to be
#    COMMITTED AND DEPLOYED — a Render deploy of an older commit rejects every
#    request from the app with no Access-Control-Allow-Origin header, which
#    also surfaces as "Network error". Verify:
#      curl -sX OPTIONS https://snowfall-server-p974.onrender.com/api/v1/auth/login \
#        -H "Origin: https://localhost" -H "Access-Control-Request-Method: POST" -D - \
#        | grep -i access-control-allow-origin
# 2. On Render's free tier the service sleeps after inactivity and the first
#    request takes ~50s to wake it, which can read as a timeout. Retry once.
# 3. Vite inlines this value AT BUILD TIME — after editing this file you must
#    re-run `npm run mobile:sync`, not just restart the app.
#
# To develop against a server running on this PC instead, comment out the line
# above and use your machine's IPv4 address (`ipconfig`), e.g.
#   VITE_API_URL=http://192.168.59.137:4001
# That only works in a DEBUG build with the phone on the same Wi-Fi, because
# cleartext HTTP is permitted solely by the debug manifest.
